  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Urgent Need for Emergency Shelters, Protection, and Assistance for Vulnerable Migrants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, IOM in Tunisia has witnessed a surge in assistance to migrants rescued at sea (RAS) in 43 operations, land arrivals particularly from Algeria. This resulted in a much greater need for shelter, and other assistance to meet the immediate humanitarian and protection needs of rescued, stranded, and other vulnerable migrants to prevent situations of destitution. The IOM-operated shelters for vulnerable migrants are at maximum capacity, and thus is it pertinent to secure and establish additional emergency shelters while also planning and supporting sustainable solutions. The aim of this project is to address the urgent need of emergency shelter as the migrant caseload surges in Tunisia. This project is providing protection and assistance to vulnerable migrants in the emergency context by establishing/refurbishing public/private spaces to use as temporary accommodations for vulnerable migrants. The project is also providing access to assistance and protection services in the spaces, and also establish medium term solutions to improve migrants&apos; resilience and foster empowerment in face of socioeconomic challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
